# mods.script - boot with the example mods loaded and play a level.
#
# The input is level1.script's, move for move and coordinate for coordinate;
# see that file for why the moves are relative and why a click is held. Two
# things are added: the overlay read at the menu, and the settings page at the
# end.
#
# It plays the level rather than only reaching it. An earlier version stopped
# once the level was on screen, and nothing that measures turns saw anything:
# 123 samples of a watched entity with zero bytes changed, a turn hook that
# counted 0 and an on_turn callback that never fired. The simulation does not
# start until the opening dialog is dismissed and the flyby is over, and the
# first turns arrive later still, so the run has to go as far as level1's does.

# Use the same readiness condition as level1.script. With asynchronous
# presentation, 16 seconds can still be the copyright screen: the first click
# dismisses it and the next selects Load Game, so no turn hooks ever run.
await picture>0.98 for 2000 within 60000
dump menu

# The overlay layer must be visible to the GAME's own file API, not merely
# present on disk.
readfile data\mods-example.txt overlay

moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 140
wait 700
click left 320 140
wait 3000
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 400
moveby 320 219
wait 700
click left 320 219
wait 12000
dump levelselect

moveby -2000 -2000
wait 300
moveby 605 448
wait 900
click left 605 448
wait 8000
dump level_start

# The opening dialog, then the flyby.
moveby -2000 -2000
wait 300
moveby 236 148
wait 700
click left 236 148
wait 4000
dump level_playing
wait 34000
dump flyby_over

peek 0x8e0428 179
watch 0 1
move 331 208
wait 800
click left 331 208
wait 1500
dump selected
move 350 245
wait 800
click left 350 245
wait 10000
dump ordered
wait 6000
dump before_page

# The mod layer consumes F10, so the page opens and the game never sees the key.
key F10 down
wait 200
key F10 up
wait 500
dump settings_page
key ESCAPE down
wait 200
key ESCAPE up
wait 500

# Entity slots and repeated watch samples also exist in the front end.
# Require the simulation's own counter before claiming the level was played.
expect entities>0
expect watch_samples>100
expect turn>0
quit
